---
title: 🥢 Sticky Ginger Sesame Tofu
description: Crispy baked tofu tossed in a sticky ginger-lime-sesame glaze, served over rice with roasted tenderstem broccoli.
tags:
  - vegan
  - tofu
  - asian
  - bowl
time: 35 minutes
servings: 2
---

-- Crispy tofu

Tear your block of @firm tofu{300%g} into nugget-sized pieces, then transfer to a #bowl{} with @cornflour{1%tbsp}, @salt{to taste} and @black pepper{to taste}. Coat well, then spread out evenly on a #baking sheet{}, drizzle with @oil{to taste} and bake at 200°C for ~{20%minutes}, or air fry for ~{10%minutes} -- until crispy.

-- Sticky ginger sesame glaze

While the tofu cooks, make the sauce by adding @maple syrup{1%tbsp}, @lime{1/2%item} juiced, @dark soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @ginger{1%thumb} grated, @garlic{1%clove} minced, @sesame oil{1%tsp}, @rice vinegar{1%tsp}, @cornflour{1%tsp} and @water{3%tbsp} to a small #jar{} and shaking to combine.

-- Roasted broccoli

When the tofu has about ~{10%minutes} remaining, spread @tenderstem broccoli{200%g} onto a #baking sheet{}, drizzle with @oil{to taste} and @salt{to taste} and bake for ~{10%minutes}.

-- Glaze and assembly

Pour the sauce into a #pan{} on a medium heat and wait until bubbling and starting to thicken. At this point, add in the crispy tofu, @spring onion{to taste}, @sesame seeds{to taste} and @red chilli{to taste}, and stir to coat.

Serve up the sticky tofu with @sticky rice{to serve} and the roasted broccoli.
